# Howdy Admin

`howdy_admin` is an admin area for your app while you develop it. It is
mounted from your `dev/` entry point, beside `howdy_dev`, so it never
reaches a deployment. Depending on what you give it, it lets you:

- [browse and edit the database](/docs/admin/database), in a grid that
  follows the data as it changes
- [manage users, groups and roles](/docs/admin/users), and sign in to the
  app as any user
- [read the mail your app sends](/docs/mail/development), and preview your
  email templates
- [follow each request](/docs/admin/telemetry) as a timeline of its
  queries, calls, emails and logs
- [watch background jobs](/docs/jobs/production) as they are queued, run
  and fail, and retry or cancel them

## Install

Add the package to the dev dependencies in `gleam.toml`, next to
`howdy_dev`:

```toml
[dev_dependencies]
howdy_dev = { git = "https://github.com/howdy-gleam/howdy.git", ref = "v1.0.0", path = "howdy_dev" }
howdy_admin = { git = "https://github.com/howdy-gleam/howdy.git", ref = "v1.0.0", path = "admin" }
```

## Mounting it

`admin.mount` adds the admin's routes to the app your `dev/` entry point
serves:

```gleam
// dev/my_app_dev.gleam
import gleam/erlang/process
import howdy/admin
import howdy/dev
import my_app

pub fn main() {
  let db = my_app.open_database()
  let identity = my_app.identity(db)
  let permissions = my_app.permissions(db)
  let dashboard =
    admin.new()
    |> admin.auth(identity)
    |> admin.authorization(permissions)

  let assert Ok(_) =
    dev.start(fn() {
      my_app.app(db, identity, permissions) |> admin.mount(dashboard)
    })
  process.sleep_forever()
}
```

Run [`howdy dev`](/docs/cli/overview) and open
<http://localhost:8787/_howdy>, on whichever port your app listens on.

Build the database, auth and anything else the admin is given outside the
function `dev.start` rebuilds the app from, as here, so they are made once
and not on every reload.

## What you register is what it shows

Gleam cannot find out at runtime which packages an app uses, and there is
no registry of the values it built, so the app hands the admin what it
has:

- `admin.database(repo)` shows the tables of a Gloo Repo, on PostgreSQL or
  SQLite. See [Database browser](/docs/admin/database).
- `admin.auth(identity)` shows users and groups from
  [Howdy Auth](/docs/auth/overview). It registers auth's Repo as the
  database too, unless `admin.database` was given another. See
  [Users and roles](/docs/admin/users).
- `admin.authorization(permissions)` shows
  [roles and permissions](/docs/auth/roles). It needs `admin.auth` too,
  since roles are held by users.
- `admin.mail(box)` shows what a `howdy/mail/outbox` keeps, and
  `admin.mail_previews(previews, send_with: mailer)` shows your email
  templates. See [Outbox and previews](/docs/mail/development).
- `admin.jobs(runner)` shows the jobs of a
  [Howdy Jobs](/docs/jobs/overview) runner: each queue's jobs by state,
  its schedules, and each job with its errors. See
  [Watching jobs](/docs/jobs/production).

The first page lists what was registered, and the sidebar links to each
part. A part that was not registered is not mounted at all.

Some things need no registering, because `admin.mount` can see them in the
app itself. If the app serves an OpenAPI document with `howdy/openapi`, the
admin lists its endpoints and lets you call them, as any user. See
[Calling your API](/docs/admin/api). Mount the admin last, so it sees the
whole app.

## Options

```gleam
admin.new()
|> admin.at("/admin")
|> admin.named("Acme admin")
|> admin.database(db)
```

- `admin.at(prefix)` moves the pages from `/_howdy`. The prefix cannot be
  `/`.
- `admin.named(name)` sets the title in the sidebar, "Howdy admin" by
  default.
- `admin.allow_hosts(hosts)` changes which host names the pages answer.
  See below.
- `admin.prefix(admin)` is where the pages are, for linking to them from
  your own dev pages.

`admin.mount(app, admin)` adds every controller to the app.
`admin.controllers(admin)` gives you the controllers instead, to mount
yourself.

## Development only

There is no login. Anyone who can reach the pages can read and change
every row, and sign in to your app as anyone. These are the defences:

- It is a dev dependency, and it is mounted from `dev/`, which
  `gleam export erlang-shipment` leaves out.
- `howdy_dev` listens on loopback only.
- The pages answer `403` to any request whose `Host` is not `localhost`,
  `127.0.0.1` or `[::1]`, so a page on another site cannot reach them
  through DNS rebinding.
- Writes must come from the admin's own origin. A `POST` whose
  `Sec-Fetch-Site` or `Origin` header says another site sent it gets `403`,
  so a page you visit while the admin runs cannot post to it. Forms carry
  no CSRF token; the browser's headers do that job.

To open the admin from another machine on a network you trust, list the
exact host names it will be reached by:

```gleam
admin.new()
|> admin.allow_hosts(["localhost", "devbox.local"])
```

`allow_hosts` replaces the loopback names, and takes host names without a
port, a scheme or wildcards. `howdy_dev` has its own `dev.bind` and
`dev.allow_hosts` for the server itself. Anyone who can reach an allowed
host owns your data.
